id: pm-0zcwz6
title: "Model capture is inert in practice: zero of 35,103 recorded entries carry a model, because the declared signal for the primary harness is an environment variable that harness does not set"
description: "The recorded entry format carries agent_model and agent_model_source, the detection layer resolves a model candidate, and history writes the field when a candidate exists. All of that shipped. What did not ship is a working signal for the harness that actually drives this repository. The built-in descriptor for claude-code declares model_environment_keys of ANTHROPIC_MODEL and CLAUDE_MODEL. Neither is present in a live Claude Code session; the environment exposes CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_PID and CLAUDE_EFFORT, and no model variable at all. The consequence is measurable rather than theoretical: scanning all 2,085 history streams and 35,103 recorded entries in this workspace returns zero entries carrying agent_model. Harness detection itself works correctly and is recorded on every entry as detected. So the capability reads as delivered on every surface — the type declares it, the detector resolves it, the writer persists it — and produces nothing, and no gate or check notices. Per-model attribution analytics, which depend entirely on this field, would return empty results that are indistinguishable from a fleet in which every agent happens to be unattributed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: attribution,history,identity,multi-agent,observability,provenance
created_at: "2026-07-26T11:06:52.473Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T06:23:37.361Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T06:23:19.612Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The declared signals for each supported harness are validated against what that harness actually exposes, and a signal that cannot fire is either corrected or recorded as unavailable rather than left declared; For harnesses that expose no model variable, an alternative resolution path is defined — client handshake metadata, invocation argument, or explicit configuration — so the field can be populated without the agent naming itself; A check reports the proportion of recorded entries carrying a model, per harness, so an inert signal is visible instead of silent; The check fails when a harness that declares a model signal records no model across a window of mutations, which is the condition that exists today; Model capture is exercised end to end for at least one harness in the test suite, asserting the recorded entry rather than the detector's return value; Documentation states which harnesses currently yield a model and which do not, so the analytics that consume it can distinguish absent from unattributed"
goal: provable-history
objective: "Make the recorded model a fact that is either present or explicitly known to be unavailable, never silently missing"
value: "Recording which model acted is a stated requirement for this tracker, and the mechanism has been treated as delivered since it shipped. It has never once produced a value. Everything built on per-model attribution is currently building on an empty column."
impact: "Turns model provenance from a declared capability into a measured one, and unblocks per-model attribution analytics which cannot function without it"
outcome: "Recorded entries carry the acting model wherever the harness can supply it, and the coverage is reported rather than assumed"
why_now: "Every mutation written while the signal is inert is a permanently unattributable entry, and this workspace has already written 35,103 of them"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "Added working environment, argv, and client model sources plus model capture analysis that distinguishes observed, unavailable, legacy-missing, and inert descriptors."
expected_result: Supported harness model provenance is captured when available and absence or inert sources are machine-readable.
actual_result: Installed CLI history persisted gpt-5.6-sol with override source; descriptor coverage and inert-capture negative controls pass.
